1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
Today we're going to talk about the Bible's signs of the end times.

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:07,300
Let's start with our "word of the day" — here are two characters.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,300
Which one is the character for "the end"?

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,300
I think the Chinese people were really quite wise.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,600
You'll notice the character for "end" is longer on top and shorter at the bottom.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,500
See how it seems to narrow as it goes, like it's coming to a dead end?

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,200
The opposite is the character for "not yet" — narrow on top and wider at the bottom.

8
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,780
It opens up wider and wider — suddenly bright and open, a whole new horizon.

9
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:35,640
These two characters capture the hope of our gathering today.

10
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:39,240
The hope that your life turns from a dead end into a future —

11
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,280
from the end of the road,

12
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,320
into a bright and glorious future.

13
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,960
I wonder if you've been following the news.

14
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,040
Sometimes there are these terrifying scenes in the news,

15
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:55,100
and sometimes people describe them as "the end of the world."

16
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:58,420
For example, this photo here — you can see it's from a few years back.

17
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:01,500
Back in 2017, there were reports of wildfires,

18
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,340
burning fiercely, with smoke billowing up into the sky.

19
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:07,900
Or take, for instance, about half a year ago —

20
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,980
the great forest fires in Borneo, Indonesia.

21
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:12,260
They burned so intensely

22
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,540
that even though it was the middle of the day,

23
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:15,320
the whole sky had turned red.

24
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:18,900
Some described it as red as the end of the world.

25
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,500
Or take the recent pandemic —

26
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,060
over in the South Korean city of Daegu,

27
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:28,380
because of the outbreak, the whole city was almost deserted,

28
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,980
as empty and desolate as if it were doomsday.

29
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:35,820
Sometimes news reports, whether intentionally or not, end up referencing the Bible.

30
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:38,380
Here's a news item from just a week ago.

31
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:42,720
It carried a warning that the world is heading for famine.

32
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,740
And how did they describe it?

33
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:46,560
They called it a famine of biblical proportions.

34
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:51,680
That's the phrase — "a famine of biblical proportions."

35
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,880
There was even the birth of a certain calf

36
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:59,000
that stirred up all these end-of-the-world anxieties.

37
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:05,000
We'll have a chance to come back to these news stories in a little while.

38
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,000
During the pandemic I once came across this photo.

39
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,920
Whoever put masks on these stone statues certainly meant well.

40
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:15,920
But it made me think of an eight-character saying:

41
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:20,560
"the true God creates man; false gods are made by man."

42
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,760
If these stones could actually catch a virus, that would be one thing;

43
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:28,840
but false gods are made by man,

44
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,640
while the true God is the One who made man.

45
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,660
And since He created man,

46
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:33,460
and human beings have reason,

47
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:34,740
the ability to analyze,

48
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:37,040
this God, of course, has that too.

49
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,840
He's given us plenty of evidence,

50
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:41,140
so that we can know, rationally, that He is real —

51
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,420
His existence,

52
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:43,440
and how precious He is.

53
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:46,260
One of those pieces of evidence is the Bible.

54
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:49,080
The Bible is full of prophecy.

55
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:51,380
Someone has actually done the count,

56
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:54,960
and more than a quarter of the Bible is prophecy.

57
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:59,060
As the name suggests, prophecy means something that hasn't happened yet

58
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,860
is told beforehand,

59
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,640
and when the time comes,

60
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,440
it really happens just like that.

61
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,480
And so, through prophecy,

62
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:08,020
we come to know that God is real,

63
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,820
that the One the Bible speaks of is the true God.

64
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,340
At the same time,

65
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:13,400
He also wants us to be prepared.

66
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:14,420
To prepare on purpose.

67
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:15,960
When the sky is full of dark clouds,

68
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:16,720
and you're heading out,

69
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,000
wouldn't you take an umbrella?

70
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
So in the same way, through prophecy God wants us to be ready.

71
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:30,000
So does the Bible actually say anything about the last days, the end of the age?

72
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Two thousand years ago, when the Lord Jesus was on earth,

73
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
there was a time when He was together with His disciples,

74
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
and they put a question like this to the Lord Jesus.

75
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
What did they ask?

76
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
They said, "Tell us, what will be the sign of Your coming, and of the end of the age?"

77
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,840
The Bible really does tell us there is an end of the age.

78
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,640
But I want to emphasize

79
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:54,700
that this "end of the age" does not mean the end of the world,

80
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:56,500
with everyone dead.

81
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,800
It's even clearer if you look at the English.

82
00:03:59,060 --> 00:03:59,820
What does it say here?

83
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,880
"The end of the age."

84
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,920
The close of an era.

85
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:10,060
When the Bible speaks of the end of the age, it means the close of an era, the end of a stage.

86
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,120
And what does that ending involve?

87
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,640
It involves the coming of the Lord Jesus.

88
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,940
It turns out the Lord Jesus will come again,

89
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,240
and He will begin a new era.

90
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:22,860
The Lord then answered His disciples.

91
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,400
And what did He say?

92
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,420
In response to their question about the signs of the end,

93
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:28,180
the Lord said this.

94
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,100
He said, "Take heed that no one leads you astray.

95
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:32,600
For many will come in My name,

96
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,460
even claiming to be the Christ,

97
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:35,880
and they will deceive many.

98
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:39,920
And you will hear of wars and rumors of wars.

99
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,240
Nation will rise against nation,

100
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,340
and kingdom against kingdom.

101
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:45,660
There will be famines and earthquakes in various places.

102
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,980
All these are but the beginning of the birth pains."

103
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:49,260
But I want you to notice something.

104
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:52,580
The word for "disaster" in the original is "birth pains."

105
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:56,420
What does that mean? It's like a woman giving birth.

106
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:59,500
You'll notice that as she gets close to delivery,

107
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:02,300
the contractions come more and more frequently,

108
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,100
and more and more intensely.

109
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,140
That is exactly what "birth pains" means.

110
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,700
It means you won't just see these signs;

111
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:11,520
these signs will grow more and more frequent,

112
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,520
and more and more severe.

113
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:17,520
A moment ago, did we notice that news item?

114
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,520
In Daegu, South Korea, the city center looked completely deserted.

115
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,520
And why was that?

116
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:26,520
Because at the time there was a severe outbreak in Daegu,

117
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:31,520
and that outbreak mainly involved a number of large gatherings.

118
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:33,520
I think you've heard about it in the news —

119
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,520
the so-called Shincheonji church.

120
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,520
I don't know if you're aware of this,

121
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:41,520
but its founder claims to be Jesus Christ Himself.

122
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:46,820
It turns out there are more than twenty people in South Korea who claim to be Jesus Christ,

123
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:50,420
and a great many people really do listen to them.

124
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:58,540
In these opening months of 2020, the world situation has been very tense.

125
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,540
Just think of the conflict in the Persian Gulf,

126
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:04,420
the tension between the United States and Iran,

127
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:09,300
which even now, in April, still hangs heavy with the clouds of war.

128
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:14,040
So for some people, their New Year's wish might simply be world peace.

129
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,040
Besides wars, the Bible also mentions

130
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:20,040
something in particular — commotions.

131
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:23,040
"Commotions" — what does that word actually mean?

132
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:27,040
It means not only nation rising against nation, as we said,

133
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:29,040
and people against people;

134
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,040
"commotions" are a kind of disturbance,

135
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,040
some kind of unrest or upheaval.

136
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:37,040
For example, France's Yellow Vest protests, which dragged on for years,

137
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:42,420
or last year's anti-extradition-bill movement in Hong Kong.

138
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:46,260
You'll notice these kinds of unrest are happening all over the world,

139
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:49,420
and they're only getting more serious, more intense.

140
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:54,820
I don't know about this little family of cattle here —

141
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:56,420
did they ever imagine that one day,

142
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:59,280
while they were grazing, the ground all around them would suddenly cave in?

143
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:03,260
This photo is actually from an earthquake in New Zealand,

144
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:06,280
where the grassland all around just sank down

145
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,600
and collapsed into a pit.

146
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:15,240
In this chart we can see, over the past hundred years or so,

147
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:17,540
the pattern of earthquakes.

148
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:21,120
A magnitude-5-or-above earthquake is no small tremor;

149
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,400
it's a major quake.

150
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:27,020
And you can see the frequency at which these earthquakes occur

151
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:29,580
is increasing — getting more and more frequent.

152
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,140
So remember the "birth pains"?

153
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:39,140
That's why this outbreak is called a "pandemic,"

154
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:41,140
meaning a global outbreak.

155
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:45,140
You know, the word "pandemic" actually comes from the Greek,

156
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:47,140
meaning "all people" —

157
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:50,140
that is, it involves everyone.

158
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:53,140
Think about it — in the span of just two short months,

159
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:56,140
already every single country in the world,

160
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:59,140
the whole globe, has confirmed cases.

161
00:07:59,140 --> 00:08:01,140
So the Bible says

162
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,960
there will be famines and pestilences in many places.

163
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:04,980
You can see it —

164
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,780
truly, in many places.

165
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,660
There's another feature the Bible mentions about pestilence.

166
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,200
Besides being widespread,

167
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,220
it also speaks of

168
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,780
how many people die, how many are killed.

169
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,320
For example, this verse mentions

170
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:22,640
those killed by sword, by famine, and by pestilence —

171
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,700
as many as a fourth

172
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:26,220
of the population.

173
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,300
Have you ever thought about what a quarter actually means?

174
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,100
With 7.7 billion people worldwide,

175
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,440
a quarter means 1.9 billion people dead.

176
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:37,540
That's to say, China's 1.3 billion plus America's 300-some million

177
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,340
still wouldn't be enough to make up that number.

178
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:45,480
In this photo you can also see the current pandemic.

179
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,260
You'll notice a whole lot of names.

180
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:52,380
These infectious diseases all appeared after the year 2000 — that is, within just these twenty years.

181
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:58,780
Whether it's cholera, swine flu, meningitis, SARS, measles, or Ebola,

182
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:01,080
and also MERS from the Middle East.

183
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,860
This shatters a common myth.

184
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:06,440
Some people think that in the 21st century, with medicine so advanced,

185
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,040
we simply wouldn't see plagues like these.

186
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,300
But look — in just twenty short years,

187
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,020
there have been so many plagues and infectious diseases.

188
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:16,420
And this current pneumonia —

189
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:19,400
think about it, by March the 19th

190
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,200
nine thousand people had died.

191
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:24,360
One month later,

192
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:26,300
this is April the 20th,

193
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,880
it had already jumped from nine thousand to a hundred and seventy thousand.

194
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,680
Quite frightening, really.

195
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:35,260
In the table below — I checked it yesterday —

196
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:39,860
by April the 30th, over three million people worldwide had been infected,

197
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,420
with more than 230,000 deaths.

198
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:44,740
That number, of course, is not small.

199
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:49,080
But if you compare it to the world's population of 7.7 billion,

200
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:52,920
those infected are actually only about 0.04%.

201
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,460
What does that mean?

202
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:57,220
Out of ten thousand people, only four are infected.

203
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,220
As for deaths, only three out of every hundred thousand.

204
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:02,520
Some people put it this way:

205
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:04,520
if the pandemic is going to ease,

206
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,820
you'd need herd immunity,

207
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:10,020
which might mean the virus spreading to sixty or seventy percent of people

208
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:12,460
before there's any chance of it settling down.

209
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:16,980
From 0.04% to sixty or seventy percent —

210
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:18,980
there is actually still a very long road ahead.

211
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:22,440
I mentioned a moment ago

212
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,260
that the world may well face famine in the days ahead.

213
00:10:25,260 --> 00:10:28,580
Why describe it as "a famine of biblical proportions"?

214
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:30,880
It's saying that this famine will be severe,

215
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,200
and that it will happen in many places.

216
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:35,240
In fact, I've read some of the reports —

217
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,260
right now it's already very serious.

218
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,280
What is it?

219
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:40,880
It's that in many places, the farms and the produce —

220
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,920
because of the pandemic —

221
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,960
have no workers to bring in the harvest.

222
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:48,300
Some crops are harvested, but there's no one to buy them,

223
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,580
and even once they're gathered,

224
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:50,860
there's no way to transport them,

225
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:51,880
because there are no planes,

226
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,160
no shipping.

227
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,740
As a result, a great deal of produce simply has to be dumped.

228
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:59,560
For instance, America poured away huge amounts of milk;

229
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:03,400
mainland China culled large numbers of chicks;

230
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:08,260
and Europe had to destroy a lot of its produce.

231
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:10,560
You can foresee that, in the near future,

232
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,620
perhaps within the next two or three months,

233
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:15,680
there could be famine around the world.

234
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:18,760
On top of that, you may have heard, over these past few months,

235
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:21,320
about the desert locusts.

236
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:25,220
This locust outbreak is the worst in seventy years.

237
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:28,660
It's affected, for example, the situation across Africa —

238
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:32,260
Somalia, Kenya, Ethiopia —

239
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:34,060
reaching the Arabian Peninsula,

240
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:38,720
and the locusts have even flown into Pakistan and Afghanistan.

241
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,560
Some people worry:

242
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:43,680
will the locusts actually make it to China?

243
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,060
Will they invade China?

244
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:46,920
If they got into China, that would be a huge problem —

245
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:47,920
with such an enormous population.

246
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:50,760
But then some people say,

247
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,040
"Don't worry, don't worry, don't worry —"

248
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,340
because the locusts over in China

249
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,400
wouldn't dare fly around four in a row.

250
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,980
And it's not because of any gathering restrictions —

251
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,280
it's because they'd get flattened and turned into skewers.

252
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,380
Now, there's yet another recent piece of news.

253
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:10,220
It's about the five countries down the lower Mekong River —

254
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:12,260
places like Vietnam, Cambodia,

255
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:14,560
Thailand, and Myanmar.

256
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,880
These are all traditional breadbaskets.

257
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,660
But because the Mekong's

258
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:20,460
water levels have dropped —

259
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,940
look at those photos —

260
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,540
the riverbed is left completely exposed,

261
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:27,380
bringing drought to these downstream countries.

262
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,660
But this time,

263
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:30,180
it's actually not a natural drought.

264
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:33,780
It's mainly because China built dams up in Yunnan,

265
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:34,800
to generate hydroelectric power,

266
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:36,340
and that holds back all the water.

267
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:38,640
And this actually gets us thinking about a bigger issue.

268
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:41,200
The fact is, most of the world's rivers today

269
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,240
draw their water from the high mountains,

270
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:46,320
like the Tibetan Plateau.

271
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,100
And because of global warming,

272
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,920
a great many mountain glaciers are melting.

273
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,920
You can just imagine —

274
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,920
if the water tower itself runs dry,

275
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,920
where will the rivers downstream get their water?

276
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,920
And if there's no water,

277
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,920
then the crops simply can't be irrigated.

278
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,920
So this is a huge, looming

279
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,920
crisis over our food supply.

280
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:11,920
I don't know if you've been following this news lately.

281
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,920
Scientists were really quite alarmed,

282
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,920
because up over the North Pole, in the northern hemisphere,

283
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,320
a very large ozone hole had opened up.

284
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:25,640
Ozone actually serves to hold back the sun's ultraviolet rays.

285
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:28,360
If ultraviolet light reaches the ground,

286
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:32,640
and strikes a person, it can cause skin cancer and cataracts.

287
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:36,600
Ultraviolet light also damages crops just the same,

288
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:40,480
so this, too, ends up affecting the food supply.

289
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,280
But — and this is precious —

290
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:47,460
this ozone hole healed back up very quickly, within a month.

291
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,720
And the main reason was simply that the weather warmed up.

292
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:54,560
When I think about it, I really feel God is merciful.

293
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:59,440
The warming weather let the ozone hole close back up quickly,

294
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,280
and at the same time, because of the warmer weather,

295
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:05,840
the pandemic in the northern hemisphere showed some signs of easing too.

296
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,720
Do you all remember these two photos from earlier?

297
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:17,160
It turns out the Bible tells us that on the eve of the Lord's return,

298
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:22,820
the earth will be greatly shaken, the sun will turn black like sackcloth,

299
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,260
and the full moon will become like blood.

300
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:29,260
I don't believe there's anything wrong with the sun or the moon themselves;

301
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,680
I believe it's the atmosphere that has been affected.

302
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:36,120
This same passage goes on to say

303
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:40,160
that it's not only the sun and the moon —

304
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,920
it also says the stars of heaven will fall to the earth,

305
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:46,040
like a fig tree shaken by a strong wind,

306
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,040
dropping its unripe figs.

307
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,320
You might be wondering,

308
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:53,000
what stars, falling?

309
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,960
I don't believe it's talking about Venus or Mars —

310
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,960
if those came crashing down, it would all be over.

311
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,960
Back in 2018,

312
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:03,280
China's space station,

313
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,960
Tiangong-1, came to the very end of its journey

314
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:08,360
and fell back down to earth,

315
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,560
burning up from the friction in the atmosphere,

316
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,920
and breaking apart as well.

317
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:14,920
The photo you see there shows exactly that scene.

318
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:16,920
It's just like the stars falling from heaven.

319
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,760
Just this past week —

320
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,400
I don't know if you caught this news —

321
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:27,120
there's a project called Starlink.

322
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,040
Its plan

323
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,400
is to put twelve thousand satellites up into space,

324
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,600
to blanket the whole globe,

325
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,080
so that everyone can use their phone

326
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,280
to get online directly through the satellites.

327
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:42,960
As of now they've already launched over four hundred satellites.

328
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:49,620
Now, as you know, if they're too high up they're hard to reach,

329
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,680
so they're kept fairly low —

330
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:54,740
about 300 kilometers above the ground,

331
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,800
a bit over two hundred miles.

332
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:00,380
Now, if these satellites were ever to fail —

333
00:16:00,380 --> 00:16:03,960
you see, the biggest danger with a satellite isn't its size,

334
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,980
it's its speed.

335
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:09,980
These satellites circle the whole earth in just forty-five minutes.

336
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,740
So if something ever went wrong with them,

337
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:17,340
all the satellites at that same altitude would come sweeping into one another,

338
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,980
setting off a chain reaction.

339
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:24,480
I don't know if you've ever seen the film Gravity —

340
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,480
that is exactly the problem it's about.

341
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:29,180
I imagine if they went sweeping across like that,

342
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:32,580
the whole sky would be full of stars falling from heaven.

343
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:38,560
Then, for example, there's the birth of that calf we mentioned earlier.

344
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,360
Why was it such a sensation?

345
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:44,960
Beyond the fact that for two thousand years not a single red heifer had been born,

346
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:48,800
the main reason really has to do with the people of Israel.

347
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:52,380
What they long for more than anything is to rebuild the temple

348
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:53,920
and to restore the sacrifices.

349
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:57,760
But if they are to rebuild the temple,

350
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,840
where must it be built? It must be built in Jerusalem.

351
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:02,380
And even once it's built,

352
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:07,380
they still have to purify the temple and purify the priests before they can offer sacrifices.

353
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:11,380
And that red heifer is precisely what's used for the purification.

354
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:15,380
They take the heifer — about two or three years old — and burn it to ashes,

355
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:23,380
and use its ashes to purify the temple vessels, purify the priests, and restore the sacrifices.

356
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:27,380
So for two thousand years they could never find a red heifer,

357
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,380
and when a red heifer finally appears,

358
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:33,000
in the minds of many Jews, the time to rebuild the temple has come.

359
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,280
If you take a look at the news,

360
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:42,080
America's whole strategy toward Israel has actually shifted lately.

361
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:45,580
It moved its embassy to Jerusalem.

362
00:17:45,580 --> 00:17:48,840
He's really set on brokering peace in the Middle East.

363
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:54,680
So have you heard of the "Deal of the Century," meant to bring about peace between Israel and Palestine?

364
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:58,220
This agreement is certain to come about one day,

365
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:01,160
though not necessarily led by America.

366
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:05,800
When it is achieved, and they're able to rebuild the temple

367
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:08,640
and restore the sacrifices — I would really love to see it.

368
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:13,160
When they offer up the heifer and burn it to ashes — why does that matter?

369
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:16,100
Because from where they choose to make the offering,

370
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:17,520
it also lets us know

371
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:20,020
where, in their minds, the temple is meant to stand.

372
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:25,040
So we'll just wait and watch for it.

373
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:29,900
Now, we know that two points can be joined into a straight line.

374
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:33,240
And if a great many points

375
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:35,540
all fall along one straight line,

376
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:36,820
then we can see

377
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,860
that the direction is a settled one.

378
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:41,680
When you look at all the signs we've just gone through —

379
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:42,960
false christs,

380
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:43,980
wars,

381
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,000
commotions,

382
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:46,800
earthquakes, famines, and plagues,

383
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,340
the changes in the sun, the moon, and the stars,

384
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:49,880
the things concerning the people of Israel,

385
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,660
the rebuilding of the temple, and so on —

386
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,460
you'll find that all of it is pointing in one single direction.

387
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:54,220
And what is it?

388
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:56,520
It's that the Lord Jesus is coming back.

389
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:58,580
The Lord Jesus is coming back very soon.

390
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:02,160
May we be ready to meet the Lord.

